          "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1c3ZxUaPUKayZzwkv4lGkuhJo9wUxVz7W/view",
          "totalPages": 34,
          "rawText": "FILE: Immunology-SLE.pdf\nFOLDER: Chapter 4 Immunology\nDRIVE_URL: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1c3ZxUaPUKayZzwkv4lGkuhJo9wUxVz7W/view\nTOTAL_PAGES: 34\n\n--- [Page 1] ---\nPHARMACOTHERAPY\nSLE\nin\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN\nPHARM.D., DIP CLIN EPI.\nFELLOW OF THE COLLEGE OF COMMUNITY PHARMACY (FCCP)\nCERTIFICATE OF PHARMACY (PHARMACOGENOMIC AND PRECISION MEDICINE)\n\n--- [Page 2] ---\nIntroduction\n■ Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) is an \nautoimmune disease associated with \nautoantibody production\n■ SLE is generally considered to occur most \nfrequently in women of reproductive age\n■ The exact etiology for SLE is unknown\n■ Predisposing factors: Genetic, hormone, \ncigarette smoke, Ultraviolet light, Infection \n(Epstein-Barr virus: EBV) , Psychological stress \nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 3] ---\nPathophysiology\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 4] ---\nTrigger factors\n■ Estrogen\n■ Infection\n■ Chemical or medication\n■ UV light (UV-A and B)\n■ Stress or comorbidity\nDrug induced SLE\nHydralazine\nProcainamide\nMinocycline\nChlorpromazine\nIsoniazid\nPenicillamine\nMethyldopa\nInterferon-alpha\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 5] ---\nDiagnosis\n■ อย่างน้อย 4 จาก 11 ข้อ\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 6] ---\nDiagnosis\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 7] ---\nDiagnosis\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 8] ---\nDiagnosis\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 9] ---\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n*Note: In an assay with at least 90%\nspecificity against relevant disease\ncontrols.\n\n--- [Page 10] ---\nClinical presentation\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 11] ---\nClinical presentation\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n■ Hematuria\n■ Chest pain\n■ Myopathy and fatigue\n■ Nausea, vomiting, anorexia, weight loss\n■ Joint pain, swelling\n■ Oral ulcer\n■ Rash, alopecia\n\n--- [Page 12] ---\nClinical presentation\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n■ Non-renal SLE\n■ Lupus nephritis\nEULAR recommendations for the management of SLE: 2023 update\n\n--- [Page 13] ---\nLaboratory test\n■ CBC, blood smear examination, ESR\n■ Urinalysis\n■ Chest X-ray\n■ FBS, Cr, liver function and serum albumin\n■ Stool exam (for parasite and occult blood)\n■ Antinuclear antibody (ANA)  \n■ Anti-ds DNA \n■ Anti-Sm\n■ VDRL\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nการตรวจอื่นๆ ตามอาการแสดง\nตามระบบต่างๆ\n\n--- [Page 14] ---\nSeverity\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 15] ---\nTreatment\n■ อาการน้อย\n– อาการทางผิวหนัง แผลในปาก หรือปวดข้อ ที่ไม่รุนแรง ไข้ต ่า ๆ ค่า \nlab ผิดปกติเล็กน้อย ปวดศีรษะ\n■ อาการปานกลาง\n– acute cutaneous rash, มีไข้สูง, น ้าหนักลด, serositis, พบความ\nผิดปกติของจ านวน antibody มาก, anemia\n■ อาการรุนแรง\n– มีอาการแสดงของอวัยวะส าคัญภายใน เช่น ไตอักเสบบริเวณกว้า ง \nอาการทางสมอง ชัก สับสน หมดสติ peripheral gangrene \nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 16] ---\nTreatment\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 17] ---\nTreatment\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nEULAR recommendations for the management of SLE: 2023 update\n\n--- [Page 18] ---\nTreatment\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nEULAR recommendations for the management of SLE: 2023 update\n\n--- [Page 19] ---\nTreatment\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nEULAR recommendations for the management of SLE: 2023 update\n\n--- [Page 20] ---\nTreatment\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nEULAR recommendations for the management of SLE: 2023 update\n\n--- [Page 21] ---\nTreatment\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\nTopical therapies for cutaneous lupus\n\n--- [Page 22] ---\nHydroxychloroquine\n■ Recommended for all patients.\n■ Target dose of 5 mg/kg real body weight/day.\n■ Monitoring: renal toxicity\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 23] ---\nGlucocorticoid\n■ Prescribe glucocorticoids promptly to obtain \nrapid control of inflammation using the lowest \ndose for the shortest duration and initiate \nimmunosuppressive therapy early to minimize \nglucocorticoid-related toxicity.\n■ In people with organ - or life -threatening SLE \nflares, we conditionally recommend pulse \nmethylprednisolone treatment (250–1,000 mg \nfor 1 –3 days) followed by oral glucocorticoid \ntaper.\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 24] ---\nGlucocorticoid\n■ In people with stable controlled SLE taking \nprednisone >5 mg/day, we strongly \nrecommend tapering the prednisone to a dose \nof ≤5 mg/day (and ideally discontinue \nprednisone) within 6 months. \n■ In people with sustained remission taking \nprednisone ≤5 mg/day, we conditionally \nrecommend a slow taper toward prednisone \ndiscontinuation. \n■ In people unable to taper prednisone to ≤5 \nmg/day, we conditionally recommend initiating \nor escalating immunosuppressive therapy.\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 25] ---\nPregnancy\n■ Drugs used to control the SLE should be those \nsuch as hydroxychloroquine, which can be \ncontinued throughout the pregnancy and may \ndecrease the incidence of flares\n■ Any potentially teratogenic drugs ( eg, \nmethotrexate, cyclophosphamide) should be \nstopped at least 3 months before attempting \npregnancy\n■ If corticosteroids are needed, maintenance doses \nshould be kept at the equivalent of prednisone 10 \nmg daily or less to decrease the risk of gestational \ndiabetes mellitus, infections, and premature \nrupture of membranes\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 26] ---\nMonitoring\n■ Clinical presentation\n■ Proteinuria, urine sedimentation\n■ BUN, creatinine, 24 hr urine protein and \ncreatinine clearance\n■ Other….\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 27] ---\nMonitoring\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 28] ---\nMonitoring\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 29] ---\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 30] ---\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 31] ---\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nACR guideline 2025\n\n--- [Page 32] ---\nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\n\n--- [Page 33] ---\nNon-pharmacotherapy\n■ Sun protection\n■ Smoking cessation\n■ Healthy\n■ Balanced diet\n■ Sleep hygiene\n■ Regular exercise \n■ Measures to promote bone health \nCOPYRIGHT © PAHRMA PLUS  ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\nEULAR recommendations for the management of SLE: 2023 update"
