          "rawText": "FILE: EENT-Contact lens.pdf\nFOLDER: Chapter 16 EENT\nDRIVE_URL: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PxDPDoIERBimbUevZOCN8kaRckGqDfhl/view\nTOTAL_PAGES: 7\n\n--- [Page 1] ---\nCONTACT LENS\nPONGSIRI KULCHANAWICHIEN, PHARM.D.\nPHARMA PLUS INSTITUTE\n\n--- [Page 2] ---\nIntroduction\n■ A contact lens, or simply contact, is a thin lens placed \ndirectly on the surface of the eye. \n■ Contact lenses are considered medical devices and can be \nworn to correct vision, or for cosmetic or therapeutic reasons.\n2\n\n--- [Page 3] ---\nType of contact lens\n■ Soft contact lens\n■ Rigid gas-permeable lens (RGP) or hard contact lens\n3\n\n--- [Page 4] ---\nType of contact lens\nRigid gas-permeable lens (RGP) \n➢Oxygen transmission\n➢Visual acuity\n➢Not expensive\n4\n\n--- [Page 5] ---\nType of contact lens\nSoft contact lens\n➢“Silicone hydrogel”\n➢Convenience\n➢Absorb water\n5\n\n--- [Page 6] ---\nComplication\n■ Xerophthalmia\n■ Conjunctivitis\n■ Blepharitis\n■ Inflammation\n■ Infection\n6"
